This is the classic flask-smorest MethodView argument-ordering gotcha. @blp.arguments injects the parsed/validated payload as a positional argument immediately after self, before any URL path arguments - it doesn't look at your parameter names. So Flask ends up trying to satisfy todo_id both positionally and as a keyword from the route, which collides. Fix the signature order so the injected schema data comes first, then the path parameter:

@blp.arguments(TodoUpdateSchema)
@blp.response(200, TodoSchema)
def put(self, todo_data, todo_id):
    todo = TodoModel.query.get(todo_id)
    ...

Rule of thumb: with flask-smorest/flask-restful MethodView plus @blp.arguments, decorator-injected arguments always go before the URL rule's own variables in the method signature. The 422 you mentioned is a separate, prior validation failure; once the signature order is correct the handler will actually run and that should resolve too.
